cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ShapeComplexity in your research, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "ShapeComplexity: edge amount and macro-shape complexity of leaf outlines"
abstract: >-
  ShapeComplexity is a Rust tool (command line, GUI and library) that measures
  two properties of a leaf outline from an image mask: edge amount (EA), the
  extra length of the margin profile around a smoothed blade line, which grows
  with teeth; and macro-shape complexity (MC), the summed log excess of
  elliptic Fourier fitting errors of the whitened blade line over a tolerance,
  which grows with lobes. It also reports blade elongation and petiole length.
  Version 2.0.0 replaces the entropy-based metrics of version 1.0.0.
type: software
version: 2.0.0
# date-released: set at the v2.0.0 release (step M5), together with its version DOI
license: MIT
